{
 "hash": "030cc750741af8",
 "text": "So every day, I carried his books and did his homework while the whole hallway watched. Nobody helps a Level 1. Then one night, as I finished Dex's homework at midnight, the air in my room started to hum. A blue window floated right in front of my face. It said: Secret Quest. One hundred push-ups before five A.M. Penalty: stay Level 1 forever. I'm not strong. I did eleven push-ups before my arms gave out. Then one more. Then one more. At exactly five A.M., the clock flashed, and my number changed. Level 2. Nobody has ever been happier about a two. So I kept going. Push-ups at dawn. Sprints in the rain. Pull-ups on the park bar until my palms burned. Every morning, a new quest. Level fifteen. Level forty. By spring, Level eighty-five. My arms grew. My legs stopped shaking. I started catching Dex's thrown books one-handed. But at school, I kept my hoodie up and my number hidden. Dex still thought I was Level 1, and I let him.",
 "voice": "leo",
 "lead": 0,
